  "statement": "The Harness prints what Run will do before it is pressed - the project directory and whether it is an isolated worktree, the execution policy, the lead model and the sub-agent critic, and the workflow with the three settings that used to hide inside a collapsed group - read from the controls the run payload reads; the collapsed group states its own contents and says in words when one was changed; Run's disabled state and the sentence beside it come from one predicate, so a missing task is a sentence rather than silence and a second run cannot start while one is in flight; and when Chat hands a conversation over, a banner says what it carried and where this run departs from it, and goes when the task it describes is consumed.",
