  "findings": [],
  "limits": [
    "the plan describes the payload, not the server's reading of it: an empty directory is sent empty and the run falls back to the configured project root, which the row states rather than guessing",
    "the plan covers the turn path's payload in full and the GSD and SDLC paths' extra fields (wave plan, story count) stay in their own surfaces; the nine controls they share with the turn are the ones the plan prints",
    "the HARNESS_POLICY_EFFECT table this story first introduced was removed: the selected option's own label is the description, so there is exactly one sentence about what a policy permits",
    "the advanced settings are summarised in the workflow row rather than given a fifth row, because they shape the same decision and a longer plan is a plan a reader skips",
    "the brief banner is a carry, not a promise: it compares the model and the directory the reply was sent with against the plan as it stands now, and says 'changes' when they differ - it never claims the conversation will fit"
  ]
